15 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a study process: introduction, demographic questionnaire, random order of three clinical scenarios each followed by a random interface, then phase questionnaires, all ending with an exit questionnaire.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Bar charts compare five antidepressants\204escitalopram, sertraline, bupropion, venlafaxine, and mirtazapine\204on remission rate, weight gain, sexual dysfunction, and fatigue and sedation. Mirtazapine shows highest weight gain and sedation; sertraline shows highest remission rate; bupropion has lowest side effects. Data is grouped both by criterion and by medication.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Drug comparison table lists five medications ranked by weighted score: bupropion 0.91, escitalopram 0.88, venlafaxine 0.79, mirtazapine 0.73, and sertraline 0.71. Adjacent bar chart visualizes weighted scores for each drug, broken down by fatigue and sedation, sexual dysfunction, weight gain, and remission components, with a color-coded legend. Explanatory text notes that scores range from zero to one, with higher scores indicating greater overall benefit based on normalized weighted averages for four clinical outcomes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Screenshot of a medical decision-making interface showing sliders for rating the importance of four outcomes: probability of remission, avoiding weight gain, avoiding sexual dysfunction, and avoiding fatigue and sedation. All sliders are set to five on a zero to ten scale. A \215Generate Recommendations\216 button appears at the bottom.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing perceived clinical utility scores, ranging from one to five, for three weighting methods: implicit weighting \(blue\), clinician-determined weighting \(orange\), and expert-derived weighting \(gray\) as rated by all clinicians, psychiatrists, and primary care physicians. Clinician-determined weighting receives the highest perceived utility across all groups, followed by expert-derived, and then implicit weighting. Error bars show variability within each group.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
